# Reverse pair certificates landing in the second centralizer core

The existing odd-product conjugators for census representatives 3 and 9
send the marked first involution to the second kernel words 82 and 996.
Every displayed packed product is checked by Lean's kernel. These identities
are consumed by `SecondPairs`; they do not assume a character table.

Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), p.487, Lemma 1.1.3 and Corollary 1.1.4.
The original ATLAS word/matrix attribution is retained in the imported
LocalInvolutionCensus/Fusion/source/README.md and KernelCount.Tables.
-/

